# This repository is the backend plus the deployment tooling. The frontend is a separate
# repository (learne-frontend) cloned side by side in this same folder, because deploy/build.ps1
# reaches into ../learnE-Frontend/dist to package the UI into the jar.
learnE-Frontend/

# Database dumps taken before migrations. They contain real user rows — email addresses and
# bcrypt password hashes — so they stay on disk and out of version control, private repo or not.
backups/

# Personal documents that happen to be sitting in the project folder. A CV carries a phone
# number, an address and a date of birth; nothing about it belongs in a code repository, private
# or not, and one `git add -A` would put it there.
*.pdf

# Claude Code permission overrides are per-machine, never shared.
.claude/settings.local.json
